※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=3 diag=none

※ A bundle is reached through the name a module was imported under, which is how
※ every other thing a module holds is reached -- so this needs no notation of
※ its own.
※
※ `steppable` requires an operation the module keeps to itself.  That is right
※ and is the point of resolving a bundle's lines where it was written: a
※ requirement is part of what that file said, and what a file applying it can
※ name is nobody's business but its own.

let shapes := ⎕import("shapes")

fn bigger(a: T', b: T') → T' pre(shapes.number(T')) pre(shapes.steppable(T')):
    a ⌈ b

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(bigger(2u8, 3u8), ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
